(typeof module==="object"&&module.exports?require("../curriculum.js"):BodyguardCurriculum).register(5,[["q5-801547214dd1","s5.0-c8879414c447","5.0","Introduction","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nskin and its accessory structures","integumentary system",["sebaceous gland","papillary layer","Merkel cell"],"integumentary system: skin and its accessory structures.","The answer begins with I and has 2 words.","eip-id1171731410480","f-abb5e96e6552"],["q5-272da2e65b06","s5.1-808ed5332334","5.1","Integumentary System","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\ngenetic disorder that affects the skin, in which there is no melanin production","albinism",["epidermis","hypodermis","keratinocyte"],"albinism: genetic disorder that affects the skin, in which there is no melanin production.","The answer begins with A and has 1 word.","fs-id1178368","f-965b964af172"],["q5-6f9f38cd5dff","s5.1-7162eeffe485","5.1","Stratum Basale","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\ntype of stem cell found in the stratum basale and in the hair matrix that continually undergoes cell division, producing the keratinocytes of the epidermis","basal cell",["stratum spinosum","stratum granulosum","reticular layer"],"basal cell: type of stem cell found in the stratum basale and in the hair matrix that continually undergoes cell division, producing the keratinocytes of the epidermis.","The answer begins with B and has 2 words.","fs-id1059498","f-73e2292e5fd0"],["q5-1f75efd2eb50","s5.1-9718bf68e23f","5.1","Stratum Basale","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\n(plural = dermal papillae) extension of the papillary layer of the dermis that increases surface contact between the epidermis and dermis","dermal papilla",["reticular layer","stratum corneum","stratum granulosum"],"dermal papilla: (plural = dermal papillae) extension of the papillary layer of the dermis that increases surface contact between the epidermis and dermis.","The answer begins with D and has 2 words.","fs-id1488184","f-dcc8cbbc5a37"],["q5-76bf5bed674e","s5.1-cecc8d5808c5","5.1","Layers of the Skin","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nlayer of skin between the epidermis and hypodermis, composed mainly of connective tissue and containing blood vessels, hair follicles, sweat glands, and other structures","dermis",["keratohyalin","desmosome","keratin"],"dermis: layer of skin between the epidermis and hypodermis, composed mainly of connective tissue and containing blood vessels, hair follicles, sweat glands, and other structures.","The answer begins with D and has 1 word.","fig-ch05_01_01","f-2495e98b1ea4"],["q5-30bf98b0272d","s5.1-fe793560b04b","5.1","Stratum Spinosum","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nstructure that forms an impermeable junction between cells","desmosome",["albinism","vitiligo","melanosome"],"desmosome: structure that forms an impermeable junction between cells.","The answer begins with D and has 1 word.","fs-id1689574","f-f33ec4cab265"],["q5-747dae752016","s5.1-8e2c92e1363e","5.1","Papillary Layer","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nfibers made of the protein elastin that increase the elasticity of the dermis","elastin fibers",["stratum basale","Merkel cell","Langerhans cell"],"elastin fibers: fibers made of the protein elastin that increase the elasticity of the dermis.","The answer begins with E and has 2 words.","fs-id1198448","f-17e417611d12"],["q5-5d0f3c4b0c2e","s5.1-bafd3e0b93aa","5.1","Layers of the Skin","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\noutermost tissue layer of the skin","epidermis",["melanin","keratinocyte","albinism"],"epidermis: outermost tissue layer of the skin.","The answer begins with E and has 1 word.","fig-ch05_01_01","f-11c4b85d8e2a"],["q5-1c400a1916e9","s5.1-bc70b0511b26","5.1","Layers of the Skin","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nkeratinous filament growing out of the epidermis","hair",["desmosome","keratin","melanocyte"],"hair: keratinous filament growing out of the epidermis.","The answer begins with H and has 1 word.","fig-ch05_01_01","f-264dc13ed077"],["q5-db23e6585917","s5.1-ea0819c91eba","5.1","Layers of the Skin","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nconnective tissue connecting the integument to the underlying bone and muscle","hypodermis",["epidermis","keratin","desmosome"],"hypodermis: connective tissue connecting the integument to the underlying bone and muscle.","The answer begins with H and has 1 word.","fig-ch05_01_01","f-1cc50a4a3d73"],["q5-789391dc56c7","s5.1-7e6bed95b9c6","5.1","The Epidermis","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\ntype of structural protein that gives skin, hair, and nails its hard, water-resistant properties","keratin",["melanin","vitiligo","hypodermis"],"keratin: type of structural protein that gives skin, hair, and nails its hard, water-resistant properties.","The answer begins with K and has 1 word.","fs-id1282569","f-1513509971c4"],["q5-c93d089c791a","s5.1-ef8adcaf9548","5.1","The Epidermis","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\ncell that produces keratin and is the most predominant type of cell found in the epidermis","keratinocyte",["hypodermis","melanosome","keratohyalin"],"keratinocyte: cell that produces keratin and is the most predominant type of cell found in the epidermis.","The answer begins with K and has 1 word.","fs-id1282569","f-7dbcab51ff8b"],["q5-92960c5eb08e","s5.1-0a376fb621e7","5.1","Stratum Granulosum","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\ngranulated protein found in the stratum granulosum","keratohyalin",["epidermis","keratin","vitiligo"],"keratohyalin: granulated protein found in the stratum granulosum.","The answer begins with K and has 1 word.","fs-id1205993","f-ba6f5cec4282"],["q5-a584be8c6a0c","s5.1-951f45ea41c5","5.1","Stratum Spinosum","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nspecialized dendritic cell found in the stratum spinosum that functions as a macrophage","Langerhans cell",["vitamin D","basal cell","elastin fibers"],"Langerhans cell: specialized dendritic cell found in the stratum spinosum that functions as a macrophage.","The answer begins with L and has 2 words.","fs-id1689574","f-ccd2141f56c3"],["q5-13f5ec6892f0","s5.1-853f525fcd76","5.1","Stratum Basale","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\npigment that determines the color of hair and skin","melanin",["keratinocyte","melanosome","melanocyte"],"melanin: pigment that determines the color of hair and skin.","The answer begins with M and has 1 word.","fs-id1059498","f-e389d7bfba2d"],["q5-0fc7ef4a2cab","s5.1-3f14f8b30147","5.1","Stratum Basale","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\ncell found in the stratum basale of the epidermis that produces the pigment melanin","melanocyte",["albinism","melanosome","vitiligo"],"melanocyte: cell found in the stratum basale of the epidermis that produces the pigment melanin.","The answer begins with M and has 1 word.","fs-id1059498","f-c2017f434b0c"],["q5-7afa59b0a6b3","s5.1-c54946b0b6cb","5.1","Pigmentation","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nintercellular vesicle that transfers melanin from melanocytes into keratinocytes of the epidermis","melanosome",["keratin","albinism","desmosome"],"melanosome: intercellular vesicle that transfers melanin from melanocytes into keratinocytes of the epidermis.","The answer begins with M and has 1 word.","fs-id1805681","f-98d4455c7740"],["q5-65a3131596d4","s5.1-90905e8f1eef","5.1","Stratum Basale","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nreceptor cell in the stratum basale of the epidermis that responds to the sense of touch","Merkel cell",["papillary layer","elastin fibers","vitamin D"],"Merkel cell: receptor cell in the stratum basale of the epidermis that responds to the sense of touch.","The answer begins with M and has 2 words.","fs-id1059498","f-3dab81c67d76"],["q5-e642ff63fd92","s5.1-59ec9cf12ad7","5.1","Stratum Basale","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nsuperficial layer of the dermis, made of loose, areolar connective tissue","papillary layer",["reticular layer","stratum spinosum","stratum corneum"],"papillary layer: superficial layer of the dermis, made of loose, areolar connective tissue.","The answer begins with P and has 2 words.","fs-id1133812","f-18a7d7b76a7f"],["q5-46f441b7fdd3","s5.1-264c37e4847b","5.1","Dermis","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\ndeeper layer of the dermis; it has a reticulated appearance due to the presence of abundant collagen and elastin fibers","reticular layer",["stratum spinosum","integumentary system","Merkel cell"],"reticular layer: deeper layer of the dermis; it has a reticulated appearance due to the presence of abundant collagen and elastin fibers.","The answer begins with R and has 2 words.","fig-ch05_01_06","f-b52c86982fff"],["q5-f150def2cb48","s5.1-deb90a264323","5.1","The Epidermis","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\ndeepest layer of the epidermis, made of epidermal stem cells","stratum basale",["elastin fibers","stratum granulosum","vitamin D"],"stratum basale: deepest layer of the epidermis, made of epidermal stem cells.","The answer begins with S and has 2 words.","fs-id1511323","f-21860b5296f1"],["q5-b3b59205bb18","s5.1-8b9bfb9b1d10","5.1","The Epidermis","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nmost superficial layer of the epidermis","stratum corneum",["elastin fibers","papillary layer","integumentary system"],"stratum corneum: most superficial layer of the epidermis.","The answer begins with S and has 2 words.","fs-id1511323","f-ff70231def33"],["q5-49c927eb73ac","s5.1-e4ca2bc34d4a","5.1","The Epidermis","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nlayer of the epidermis superficial to the stratum spinosum","stratum granulosum",["basal cell","papillary layer","elastin fibers"],"stratum granulosum: layer of the epidermis superficial to the stratum spinosum.","The answer begins with S and has 2 words.","fs-id1511323","f-7d3479371956"],["q5-d64e35638db2","s5.1-c1722bab249e","5.1","The Epidermis","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nlayer of the epidermis between the stratum granulosum and stratum corneum, found only in thick skin covering the palms, soles of the feet, and digits","stratum lucidum",["dermal papilla","integumentary system","elastin fibers"],"stratum lucidum: layer of the epidermis between the stratum granulosum and stratum corneum, found only in thick skin covering the palms, soles of the feet, and digits.","The answer begins with S and has 2 words.","fs-id1511323","f-615752ce7676"],["q5-e6952e363699","s5.1-c8378eaf0c81","5.1","The Epidermis","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nlayer of the epidermis superficial to the stratum basale, characterized by the presence of desmosomes","stratum spinosum",["Langerhans cell","stratum corneum","Merkel cell"],"stratum spinosum: layer of the epidermis superficial to the stratum basale, characterized by the presence of desmosomes.","The answer begins with S and has 2 words.","fs-id1511323","f-d0574665e992"],["q5-c6c6163d9b20","s5.1-8c56c31fbb78","5.1","Pigmentation","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\ncompound that aids absorption of calcium and phosphates in the intestine to improve bone health","vitamin D",["papillary layer","stratum granulosum","reticular layer"],"vitamin D: compound that aids absorption of calcium and phosphates in the intestine to improve bone health.","The answer begins with V and has 2 words.","fs-id1828260","f-dee82d85e6fe"],["q5-826dfdf84d88","s5.1-4bfdd483dfb5","5.1","Integumentary System","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nskin condition in which melanocytes in certain areas lose the ability to produce melanin, possibly due an autoimmune reaction that leads to loss of color in patches","vitiligo",["albinism","epidermis","keratin"],"vitiligo: skin condition in which melanocytes in certain areas lose the ability to produce melanin, possibly due an autoimmune reaction that leads to loss of color in patches.","The answer begins with V and has 1 word.","fs-id1178368","f-d2c29185f782"],["q5-843300bfa8c5","s5.1-bafd3e0b93aa","5.1","The Epidermis","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe ____ is composed of keratinized, stratified squamous epithelium.","epidermis",["vitiligo","keratohyalin","keratinocyte"],"The epidermis is composed of keratinized, stratified squamous epithelium.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1511323","f-5cec20d51e48"],["q5-1f093f6349f5","s5.1-deb90a264323","5.1","The Epidermis","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe cells in all of the layers except the ____ are called keratinocytes.","stratum basale",["dermal papilla","stratum spinosum","Langerhans cell"],"The cells in all of the layers except the stratum basale are called keratinocytes.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1282569","f-659e94d9095e"],["q5-30bff0b37c9b","s5.1-ef8adcaf9548","5.1","The Epidermis","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nA ____ is a cell that manufactures and stores the protein keratin.","keratinocyte",["melanosome","hypodermis","albinism"],"A keratinocyte is a cell that manufactures and stores the protein keratin.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1282569","f-e808612e2f56"],["q5-9528304ad52c","s5.1-8b9bfb9b1d10","5.1","The Epidermis","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe keratinocytes in the ____ are dead and regularly slough away, being replaced by cells from the deeper layers.","stratum corneum",["dermal papilla","Merkel cell","vitamin D"],"The keratinocytes in the stratum corneum are dead and regularly slough away, being replaced by cells from the deeper layers.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1282569","f-b7d82f4e63b8"],["q5-2a40487f1098","s5.1-deb90a264323","5.1","Stratum Basale","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe cells in the ____ bond to the dermis via intertwining collagen fibers, referred to as the basement membrane.","stratum basale",["reticular layer","basal cell","integumentary system"],"The cells in the stratum basale bond to the dermis via intertwining collagen fibers, referred to as the basement membrane.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1488184","f-d1747312c525"],["q5-2ddb936a8f96","s5.1-9718bf68e23f","5.1","Stratum Basale","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nA finger-like projection, or fold, known as the ____ (plural = dermal papillae) is found in the superficial portion of the dermis.","dermal papilla",["stratum spinosum","elastin fibers","Langerhans cell"],"A finger-like projection, or fold, known as the dermal papilla (plural = dermal papillae) is found in the superficial portion of the dermis.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1488184","f-19534f27d309"],["q5-0b47f62ab355","s5.1-bafd3e0b93aa","5.1","Stratum Basale","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nDermal papillae increase the strength of the connection between the ____ and dermis; the greater the folding, the stronger the connections made.","epidermis",["vitiligo","melanocyte","albinism"],"Dermal papillae increase the strength of the connection between the epidermis and dermis; the greater the folding, the stronger the connections made.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1488184","f-5d412090b6dc"],["q5-c77b1afb9532","s5.1-deb90a264323","5.1","Stratum Basale","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe ____ is a single layer of cells primarily made of basal cells.","stratum basale",["Merkel cell","stratum granulosum","basal cell"],"The stratum basale is a single layer of cells primarily made of basal cells.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1059498","f-1eb11eeed932"],["q5-6ddbae63c39e","s5.1-7162eeffe485","5.1","Stratum Basale","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nA ____ is a cuboidal-shaped stem cell that is a precursor of the keratinocytes of the epidermis.","basal cell",["stratum corneum","vitamin D","reticular layer"],"A basal cell is a cuboidal-shaped stem cell that is a precursor of the keratinocytes of the epidermis.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1059498","f-20c35f7808a6"],["q5-0cdf57641900","s5.1-deb90a264323","5.1","Stratum Basale","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nAs new cells are formed, the existing cells are pushed superficially away from the ____.","stratum basale",["elastin fibers","basal cell","Langerhans cell"],"As new cells are formed, the existing cells are pushed superficially away from the stratum basale.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1059498","f-5f922ae9662a"],["q5-37d312fc4f2e","s5.1-90905e8f1eef","5.1","Stratum Basale","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe first is a ____, which functions as a receptor and is responsible for stimulating sensory nerves that the brain perceives as touch.","Merkel cell",["elastin fibers","stratum spinosum","reticular layer"],"The first is a Merkel cell, which functions as a receptor and is responsible for stimulating sensory nerves that the brain perceives as touch.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1059498","f-a3de833cba08"],["q5-738c4892935b","s5.1-59ec9cf12ad7","5.1","Stratum Basale","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nIn a growing fetus, fingerprints form where the cells of the stratum basale meet the papillae of the underlying dermal layer (____), resulting in the formation of the ridges on your fingers that you recognize as fingerprints.","papillary layer",["stratum lucidum","elastin fibers","stratum corneum"],"In a growing fetus, fingerprints form where the cells of the stratum basale meet the papillae of the underlying dermal layer (papillary layer), resulting in the formation of the ridges on your fingers that you recognize as fingerprints.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1133812","f-7d61660be670"],["q5-1e35b21515a1","s5.1-c8378eaf0c81","5.1","Stratum Spinosum","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nAs the name suggests, the ____ is spiny in appearance due to the protruding cell processes that join the cells via a structure called a desmosome.","stratum spinosum",["Merkel cell","vitamin D","elastin fibers"],"As the name suggests, the stratum spinosum is spiny in appearance due to the protruding cell processes that join the cells via a structure called a desmosome.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1689574","f-6a843f631d2c"],["q5-9e032f490602","s5.1-c8378eaf0c81","5.1","Stratum Spinosum","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe ____ is composed of eight to 10 layers of keratinocytes, formed as a result of cell division in the stratum basale.","stratum spinosum",["papillary layer","stratum granulosum","stratum corneum"],"The stratum spinosum is composed of eight to 10 layers of keratinocytes, formed as a result of cell division in the stratum basale.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1689574","f-fa1abc37e5ce"],["q5-f1836b123199","s5.1-c8378eaf0c81","5.1","Layers of the Skin","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe keratinocytes in the ____ begin the synthesis of keratin and release a water-repelling glycolipid that helps prevent water loss from the body, making the skin relatively waterproof.","stratum spinosum",["basal cell","stratum granulosum","elastin fibers"],"The keratinocytes in the stratum spinosum begin the synthesis of keratin and release a water-repelling glycolipid that helps prevent water loss from the body, making the skin relatively waterproof.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1472511","f-1851a589f890"],["q5-f8e50a8c4e7b","s5.1-e4ca2bc34d4a","5.1","Layers of the Skin","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nAs new keratinocytes are produced atop the stratum basale, the keratinocytes of the stratum spinosum are pushed into the ____.","stratum granulosum",["dermal papilla","integumentary system","Merkel cell"],"As new keratinocytes are produced atop the stratum basale, the keratinocytes of the stratum spinosum are pushed into the stratum granulosum.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1472511","f-04c806a08f2e"],["q5-ff9f91a01f02","s5.1-c1722bab249e","5.1","Stratum Granulosum","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe nuclei and other cell organelles disintegrate as the cells die, leaving behind the keratin, keratohyalin, and cell membranes that will form the ____, the stratum corneum, and the accessory structures of hair and nails.","stratum lucidum",["basal cell","vitamin D","papillary layer"],"The nuclei and other cell organelles disintegrate as the cells die, leaving behind the keratin, keratohyalin, and cell membranes that will form the stratum lucidum, the stratum corneum, and the accessory structures of hair and nails.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1205993","f-7b2700f110f9"],["q5-2a5d73aa8c66","s5.1-c1722bab249e","5.1","Stratum Lucidum","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe keratinocytes that compose the ____ are dead and flattened.","stratum lucidum",["papillary layer","stratum granulosum","elastin fibers"],"The keratinocytes that compose the stratum lucidum are dead and flattened.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1330935","f-a90269e9384c"],["q5-13d3436ada96","s5.1-8b9bfb9b1d10","5.1","Stratum Corneum","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe ____ is the most superficial layer of the epidermis and is the layer exposed to the outside environment.","stratum corneum",["vitamin D","stratum spinosum","stratum basale"],"The stratum corneum is the most superficial layer of the epidermis and is the layer exposed to the outside environment.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1298153","f-299816fb32d2"],["q5-04a77f3f05be","s5.1-8b9bfb9b1d10","5.1","Stratum Corneum","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThere are usually 15 to 30 layers of cells in the ____.","stratum corneum",["Langerhans cell","elastin fibers","stratum lucidum"],"There are usually 15 to 30 layers of cells in the stratum corneum.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1298153","f-d615af48e7c3"],["q5-01e1276eb1c3","s5.1-cecc8d5808c5","5.1","Dermis","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe ____ is made of two layers of connective tissue that compose an interconnected mesh of elastin and collagenous fibers, produced by fibroblasts.","dermis",["melanosome","keratohyalin","melanin"],"The dermis is made of two layers of connective tissue that compose an interconnected mesh of elastin and collagenous fibers, produced by fibroblasts.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1146438","f-c03563882960"],["q5-f0c3dd5ebb91","s5.1-59ec9cf12ad7","5.1","Papillary Layer","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nWithin the ____ are fibroblasts, a small number of fat cells (adipocytes), and an abundance of small blood vessels.","papillary layer",["Langerhans cell","vitamin D","stratum basale"],"Within the papillary layer are fibroblasts, a small number of fat cells (adipocytes), and an abundance of small blood vessels.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1198448","f-39384955d3eb"],["q5-463fa5e3ef21","s5.1-59ec9cf12ad7","5.1","Papillary Layer","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe ____ contains phagocytes, defensive cells that help fight bacteria or other infections that have breached the skin.","papillary layer",["stratum corneum","vitamin D","stratum basale"],"In addition, the papillary layer contains phagocytes, defensive cells that help fight bacteria or other infections that have breached the skin.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1198448","f-aab40e694e63"],["q5-c256889a85f1","s5.1-59ec9cf12ad7","5.1","Reticular Layer","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nUnderlying the ____ is the much thicker reticular layer, composed of dense, irregular connective tissue.","papillary layer",["vitamin D","Langerhans cell","stratum spinosum"],"Underlying the papillary layer is the much thicker reticular layer, composed of dense, irregular connective tissue.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1490919","f-68d83c83f280"],["q5-e27eda107fc6","s5.1-264c37e4847b","5.1","Reticular Layer","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe ____ appears reticulated (net-like) due to a tight meshwork of fibers.","reticular layer",["basal cell","Merkel cell","Langerhans cell"],"The reticular layer appears reticulated (net-like) due to a tight meshwork of fibers.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1490919","f-891ff0d0f05f"],["q5-0608e4db6978","s5.1-8e2c92e1363e","5.1","Reticular Layer","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\n____ provide some elasticity to the skin, enabling movement.","Elastin fibers",["Merkel cell","papillary layer","basal cell"],"Elastin fibers provide some elasticity to the skin, enabling movement.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1490919","f-2d8b3a655b31"],["q5-a3113127451d","s5.1-59ec9cf12ad7","5.1","Reticular Layer","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nCollagen fibers provide structure and tensile strength, with strands of collagen extending into both the ____ and the hypodermis.","papillary layer",["vitamin D","Langerhans cell","dermal papilla"],"Collagen fibers provide structure and tensile strength, with strands of collagen extending into both the papillary layer and the hypodermis.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1490919","f-e1325284ccc8"],["q5-a565fb94547f","s5.1-cecc8d5808c5","5.1","Reticular Layer","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nCollagen injections and Retin-A creams help restore skin turgor by either introducing collagen externally or stimulating blood flow and repair of the ____, respectively.","dermis",["desmosome","keratohyalin","albinism"],"Collagen injections and Retin-A creams help restore skin turgor by either introducing collagen externally or stimulating blood flow and repair of the dermis, respectively.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1490919","f-c249d48004b8"],["q5-f00e3ab089cf","s5.1-ea0819c91eba","5.1","Hypodermis","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe ____ consists of well-vascularized, loose, areolar connective tissue and adipose tissue, which functions as a mode of fat storage and provides insulation and cushioning for the integument.","hypodermis",["epidermis","keratohyalin","keratinocyte"],"The hypodermis consists of well-vascularized, loose, areolar connective tissue and adipose tissue, which functions as a mode of fat storage and provides insulation and cushioning for the integument.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1448861","f-feecf3f5040d"],["q5-f7121c14006f","s5.1-ea0819c91eba","5.1","Lipid Storage","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nAdipose tissue present in the ____ consists of fat-storing cells called adipocytes.","hypodermis",["keratin","keratinocyte","hair"],"Adipose tissue present in the hypodermis consists of fat-storing cells called adipocytes.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1142685","f-7bbc2a3b4c5e"],["q5-d1fc3b716837","s5.1-ea0819c91eba","5.1","Lipid Storage","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nWhere the fat is deposited and accumulates within the ____ depends on hormones (testosterone, estrogen, insulin, glucagon, leptin, and others), as well as genetic factors.","hypodermis",["melanocyte","melanosome","hair"],"Where the fat is deposited and accumulates within the hypodermis depends on hormones (testosterone, estrogen, insulin, glucagon, leptin, and others), as well as genetic factors.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1318566","f-bd5d787f4876"],["q5-de1c49e10e9e","s5.1-853f525fcd76","5.1","Pigmentation","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe color of skin is influenced by a number of pigments, including ____, carotene, and hemoglobin.","melanin",["albinism","desmosome","keratin"],"The color of skin is influenced by a number of pigments, including melanin, carotene, and hemoglobin.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1805681","f-780bd68019c2"],["q5-46ed82934789","s5.1-deb90a264323","5.1","Pigmentation","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nRecall that melanin is produced by cells called melanocytes, which are found scattered throughout the ____ of the epidermis.","stratum basale",["basal cell","dermal papilla","elastin fibers"],"Recall that melanin is produced by cells called melanocytes, which are found scattered throughout the stratum basale of the epidermis.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1805681","f-e6215b7d45f0"],["q5-f3182c3a02e4","s5.1-c54946b0b6cb","5.1","Pigmentation","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe melanin is transferred into the keratinocytes via a cellular vesicle called a ____.","melanosome",["albinism","keratin","hypodermis"],"The melanin is transferred into the keratinocytes via a cellular vesicle called a melanosome.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1805681","f-7c26aeccb8af"],["q5-6d1bf902ae3d","s5.1-853f525fcd76","5.1","Pigmentation","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nExposure to the UV rays of the sun or a tanning salon causes ____ to be manufactured and built up in keratinocytes, as sun exposure stimulates keratinocytes to secrete chemicals that stimulate melanocytes.","melanin",["dermis","melanosome","desmosome"],"Exposure to the UV rays of the sun or a tanning salon causes melanin to be manufactured and built up in keratinocytes, as sun exposure stimulates keratinocytes to secrete chemicals that stimulate melanocytes.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1828260","f-3e01bd5726e2"],["q5-0f7f84472a1d","s5.1-853f525fcd76","5.1","Pigmentation","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe accumulation of ____ in keratinocytes results in the darkening of the skin, or a tan.","melanin",["vitiligo","albinism","desmosome"],"The accumulation of melanin in keratinocytes results in the darkening of the skin, or a tan.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1828260","f-d86eaf036384"],["q5-4c5433291ff4","s5.1-8c56c31fbb78","5.1","Pigmentation","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nToo much melanin can interfere with the production of ____, an important nutrient involved in calcium absorption.","vitamin D",["integumentary system","dermal papilla","elastin fibers"],"In contrast, too much melanin can interfere with the production of vitamin D, an important nutrient involved in calcium absorption.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1828260","f-441d7a5d4899"],["q5-83381190ed97","s5.1-8c56c31fbb78","5.1","Pigmentation","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThus, the amount of melanin present in our skin is dependent on a balance between available sunlight and folic acid destruction, and protection from UV radiation and ____ production.","vitamin D",["stratum corneum","elastin fibers","basal cell"],"Thus, the amount of melanin present in our skin is dependent on a balance between available sunlight and folic acid destruction, and protection from UV radiation and vitamin D production.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1828260","f-7fdb0743db32"],["q5-ab5fd862154c","s5.1-808ed5332334","5.1","Integumentary System","application","Which term correctly completes this statement?\n____ is a genetic disorder that affects (completely or partially) the coloring of skin, hair, and eyes.","Albinism",["dermis","melanocyte","hypodermis"],"Albinism is a genetic disorder that affects (completely or partially) the coloring of skin, hair, and eyes.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1523476","f-cff0d1c7bec2"],["q5-d4812dbcc3aa","s5.1-853f525fcd76","5.1","Integumentary System","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe defect is primarily due to the inability of melanocytes to produce ____.","melanin",["melanosome","melanocyte","vitiligo"],"The defect is primarily due to the inability of melanocytes to produce melanin.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1523476","f-c5aff0cedd09"],["q5-5cd68ccb3abf","s5.1-853f525fcd76","5.1","Integumentary System","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nRecall that ____ helps protect the skin from the harmful effects of UV radiation.","melanin",["albinism","hair","keratinocyte"],"Recall that melanin helps protect the skin from the harmful effects of UV radiation.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1523476","f-52fe6917daba"],["q5-414910687bd8","s5.1-808ed5332334","5.1","Integumentary System","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nNeither ____ nor vitiligo directly affects the lifespan of an individual.","albinism",["keratinocyte","keratin","melanocyte"],"Neither albinism nor vitiligo directly affects the lifespan of an individual.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1523476","f-01dc959d2143"],["q5-487fb3d4d781","s5.1-3f14f8b30147","5.1","Integumentary System","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nTumors of the pituitary gland can result in the secretion of large amounts of ____-stimulating hormone (MSH), which results in a darkening of the skin.","melanocyte",["melanosome","keratin","melanin"],"Tumors of the pituitary gland can result in the secretion of large amounts of melanocyte-stimulating hormone (MSH), which results in a darkening of the skin.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1271098","f-553d0d561b87"],["q5-d365ead6c9fc","s5.2-1ac12aa01bca","5.2","Hair Growth","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nactive phase of the hair growth cycle","anagen",["keratin","cuticle","lunula"],"anagen: active phase of the hair growth cycle.","The answer begins with A and has 1 word.","fs-id961934","f-39ee7b590b4f"],["q5-0b78758bf95e","s5.2-be80f573655d","5.2","Sweat Glands","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\ntype of sweat gland that is associated with hair follicles in the armpits and genital regions","apocrine sweat gland",["external root sheath","eccrine sweat gland","internal root sheath"],"apocrine sweat gland: type of sweat gland that is associated with hair follicles in the armpits and genital regions.","The answer begins with A and has 3 words.","fs-id1449977","f-6d3b6c0ae18a"],["q5-437811350c1e","s5.2-9bf634e35c6a","5.2","Accessory Structures of the Skin","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nsmooth muscle that is activated in response to external stimuli that pull on hair follicles and make the hair “stand up”","arrector pili",["stratum basale","hair papilla","nail cuticle"],"arrector pili: smooth muscle that is activated in response to external stimuli that pull on hair follicles and make the hair “stand up”.","The answer begins with A and has 2 words.","fs-id1500108","f-952519daf53e"],["q5-f9229fdc2e26","s5.2-89d49c040191","5.2","Hair Growth","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\ntransitional phase marking the end of the anagen phase of the hair growth cycle","catagen",["sebum","cortex","telogen"],"catagen: transitional phase marking the end of the anagen phase of the hair growth cycle.","The answer begins with C and has 1 word.","fs-id961934","f-a625f763a4ae"],["q5-8622f4b7c48c","s5.2-883ff2c19169","5.2","Hair","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nin hair, the second or middle layer of keratinocytes originating from the hair matrix, as seen in a cross-section of the hair bulb","cortex",["lunula","keratin","anagen"],"cortex: in hair, the second or middle layer of keratinocytes originating from the hair matrix, as seen in a cross-section of the hair bulb.","The answer begins with C and has 1 word.","fs-id1319983","f-5a0a55a445fc"],["q5-3f4ddfe985bd","s5.2-a5aa0c529d5e","5.2","Hair","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nin hair, the outermost layer of keratinocytes originating from the hair matrix, as seen in a cross-section of the hair bulb","cuticle",["keratin","anagen","sebum"],"cuticle: in hair, the outermost layer of keratinocytes originating from the hair matrix, as seen in a cross-section of the hair bulb.","The answer begins with C and has 1 word.","fs-id1319983","f-b895de86d67f"],["q5-776a86760a4f","s5.2-7948b63a56f7","5.2","Sweat Glands","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\ntype of sweat gland that is common throughout the skin surface; it produces a hypotonic sweat for thermoregulation","eccrine sweat gland",["external root sheath","internal root sheath","apocrine sweat gland"],"eccrine sweat gland: type of sweat gland that is common throughout the skin surface; it produces a hypotonic sweat for thermoregulation.","The answer begins with E and has 3 words.","fs-id1509858","f-020afe2987ac"],["q5-23ecbf3e634d","s5.2-0dd314595220","5.2","Nails","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nnail fold that meets the proximal end of the nail body, also called the cuticle","eponychium",["medulla","cortex","melanin"],"eponychium: nail fold that meets the proximal end of the nail body, also called the cuticle.","The answer begins with E and has 1 word.","fs-id1200286","f-9f57ac830d07"],["q5-1e71781a0e10","s5.2-08c5c1d4258d","5.2","Hair","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nouter layer of the hair follicle that is an extension of the epidermis, which encloses the hair root","external root sheath",["eccrine sweat gland","internal root sheath","apocrine sweat gland"],"external root sheath: outer layer of the hair follicle that is an extension of the epidermis, which encloses the hair root.","The answer begins with E and has 3 words.","fs-id1533651","f-beb3c48d1d08"],["q5-b830048bacd3","s5.2-18ed80d432fc","5.2","Hair","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nthe basement membrane that is found between the epithelium of the external root sheath and the connective tissue sheath","glassy membrane",["hair matrix","nail body","arrector pili"],"glassy membrane: the basement membrane that is found between the epithelium of the external root sheath and the connective tissue sheath.","The answer begins with G and has 2 words.","fs-id1533651","f-0c4a996bd6ea"],["q5-b369870652de","s5.2-f6b0a54c0899","5.2","Hair","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nstructure at the base of the hair root that surrounds the dermal papilla","hair bulb",["hair shaft","stratum basale","arrector pili"],"hair bulb: structure at the base of the hair root that surrounds the dermal papilla.","The answer begins with H and has 2 words.","fs-id1541120","f-879d9b99a799"],["q5-df272241f1d7","s5.2-76bbbc9db5e8","5.2","Hair","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\ncavity or sac from which hair originates","hair follicle",["stratum basale","arrector pili","sebaceous gland"],"hair follicle: cavity or sac from which hair originates.","The answer begins with H and has 2 words.","fs-id1541120","f-a1599bdbac9b"],["q5-0425b413d08b","s5.2-31eeb8e7f9c2","5.2","Hair","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nlayer of basal cells from which a strand of hair grows","hair matrix",["hair root","glassy membrane","nail fold"],"hair matrix: layer of basal cells from which a strand of hair grows.","The answer begins with H and has 2 words.","fs-id1541120","f-e472309ebd5b"],["q5-0f0f9a2bbf1d","s5.2-e01468886bdb","5.2","Hair","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nmass of connective tissue, blood capillaries, and nerve endings at the base of the hair follicle","hair papilla",["nail body","arrector pili","integumentary system"],"hair papilla: mass of connective tissue, blood capillaries, and nerve endings at the base of the hair follicle.","The answer begins with H and has 2 words.","fs-id1541120","f-b293cabb581f"],["q5-01760139f472","s5.2-7fd700ceab95","5.2","Hair","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\npart of hair that is below the epidermis anchored to the follicle","hair root",["sebaceous gland","nail fold","hair shaft"],"hair root: part of hair that is below the epidermis anchored to the follicle.","The answer begins with H and has 2 words.","fs-id1541120","f-4bae23d371f8"],["q5-8b14740ee787","s5.2-eb244f8e3ff9","5.2","Hair","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\npart of hair that is above the epidermis but is not anchored to the follicle","hair shaft",["sebaceous gland","stratum basale","nail body"],"hair shaft: part of hair that is above the epidermis but is not anchored to the follicle.","The answer begins with H and has 2 words.","fs-id1541120","f-71468300fe3d"],["q5-aaff77623f67","s5.2-90ab8ef22292","5.2","Nails","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nthickened layer of stratum corneum that lies below the free edge of the nail","hyponychium",["hypodermis","dermis","hair"],"hyponychium: thickened layer of stratum corneum that lies below the free edge of the nail.","The answer begins with H and has 1 word.","fs-id1200286","f-9aeebcaa19ad"],["q5-6d08656cae30","s5.2-dd544644a8cf","5.2","Hair","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\ninnermost layer of keratinocytes in the hair follicle that surround the hair root up to the hair shaft","internal root sheath",["apocrine sweat gland","external root sheath","eccrine sweat gland"],"internal root sheath: innermost layer of keratinocytes in the hair follicle that surround the hair root up to the hair shaft.","The answer begins with I and has 3 words.","fs-id1533651","f-9bcc2490cd6d"],["q5-9a1a3f81ab7b","s5.2-d002c3f75ef4","5.2","Nails","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nbasal part of the nail body that consists of a crescent-shaped layer of thick epithelium","lunula",["anagen","keratin","eponychium"],"lunula: basal part of the nail body that consists of a crescent-shaped layer of thick epithelium.","The answer begins with L and has 1 word.","fs-id1200286","f-fe108dfe050e"],["q5-e03638a22127","s5.2-4fc79783b47c","5.2","Hair","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nin hair, the innermost layer of keratinocytes originating from the hair matrix","medulla",["hypodermis","sebum","epidermis"],"medulla: in hair, the innermost layer of keratinocytes originating from the hair matrix.","The answer begins with M and has 1 word.","fs-id1319983","f-db525842e771"],["q5-6c654acee4d6","s5.2-5765ed8d7910","5.2","Nails","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nlayer of epidermis upon which the nail body forms","nail bed",["nail root","hair bulb","hair follicle"],"nail bed: layer of epidermis upon which the nail body forms.","The answer begins with N and has 2 words.","fs-id1200286","f-7609c72d334c"],["q5-1115acdb2557","s5.2-9c95b486d1e2","5.2","Nails","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nmain keratinous plate that forms the nail","nail body",["hair shaft","hair matrix","nail cuticle"],"nail body: main keratinous plate that forms the nail.","The answer begins with N and has 2 words.","fs-id1200286","f-a85f11577c5e"],["q5-fb317af95eb9","s5.2-2b53e512dbc1","5.2","Nails","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nfold of epithelium that extends over the nail bed, also called the eponychium","nail cuticle",["glassy membrane","hair bulb","hair papilla"],"nail cuticle: fold of epithelium that extends over the nail bed, also called the eponychium.","The answer begins with N and has 2 words.","fs-id1200286","f-5fb04ee099ce"],["q5-4b9af51500c6","s5.2-994b9c413f31","5.2","Nails","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nfold of epithelium at that extend over the sides of the nail body, holding it in place","nail fold",["nail root","stratum corneum","hair follicle"],"nail fold: fold of epithelium at that extend over the sides of the nail body, holding it in place.","The answer begins with N and has 2 words.","fs-id1200286","f-3cb8631c0df8"],["q5-3507579b4a71","s5.2-693de69bd1b4","5.2","Nails","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\npart of the nail that is lodged deep in the epidermis from which the nail grows","nail root",["integumentary system","hair shaft","hair follicle"],"nail root: part of the nail that is lodged deep in the epidermis from which the nail grows.","The answer begins with N and has 2 words.","fs-id1200286","f-b50af5c4b8e4"],["q5-3d6bd385aa25","s5.2-5beda771f93c","5.2","Sebaceous Glands","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\ntype of oil gland found in the dermis all over the body and helps to lubricate and waterproof the skin and hair by secreting sebum","sebaceous gland",["hair matrix","hair bulb","nail root"],"sebaceous gland: type of oil gland found in the dermis all over the body and helps to lubricate and waterproof the skin and hair by secreting sebum.","The answer begins with S and has 2 words.","fs-id1107478","f-d35da170776c"],["q5-9462f7723eb8","s5.2-da28390c7c3d","5.2","Sebaceous Glands","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\noily substance that is composed of a mixture of lipids that lubricates the skin and hair","sebum",["catagen","hypodermis","medulla"],"sebum: oily substance that is composed of a mixture of lipids that lubricates the skin and hair.","The answer begins with S and has 1 word.","fs-id1107478","f-a44a8dcf19fe"],["q5-9bbae349af63","s5.2-ccd556f8332b","5.2","Hair Growth","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nresting phase of the hair growth cycle initiated with catagen and terminated by the beginning of a new anagen phase of hair growth","telogen",["hyponychium","lunula","eponychium"],"telogen: resting phase of the hair growth cycle initiated with catagen and terminated by the beginning of a new anagen phase of hair growth.","The answer begins with T and has 1 word.","fs-id961934","f-d5ce3af10a42"],["q5-98678eb154c6","s5.2-bc70b0511b26","5.2","Accessory Structures of the Skin","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nAccessory structures of the skin include ____, nails, sweat glands, and sebaceous glands.","hair",["medulla","melanin","eponychium"],"Accessory structures of the skin include hair, nails, sweat glands, and sebaceous glands.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1539274","f-3a9b6e0f70e9"],["q5-ce500ebb1d03","s5.2-bafd3e0b93aa","5.2","Hair","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nHair is a keratinous filament growing out of the ____.","epidermis",["sebum","telogen","eponychium"],"Hair is a keratinous filament growing out of the epidermis.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1541120","f-85948c9a7cc2"],["q5-f8c01a7df9ed","s5.2-76bbbc9db5e8","5.2","Hair","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nStrands of hair originate in an epidermal penetration of the dermis called the ____.","hair follicle",["integumentary system","arrector pili","hair shaft"],"Strands of hair originate in an epidermal penetration of the dermis called the hair follicle.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1541120","f-7b04a886e4d4"],["q5-1d7658a96e0c","s5.2-31eeb8e7f9c2","5.2","Hair","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe hair root ends deep in the dermis at the hair bulb, and includes a layer of mitotically active basal cells called the ____.","hair matrix",["hair follicle","nail body","glassy membrane"],"The hair root ends deep in the dermis at the hair bulb, and includes a layer of mitotically active basal cells called the hair matrix.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1541120","f-a24b06a8f709"],["q5-9c831f0b0b75","s5.2-e01468886bdb","5.2","Hair","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe hair bulb surrounds the ____, which is made of connective tissue and contains blood capillaries and nerve endings from the dermis.","hair papilla",["nail body","stratum basale","hair root"],"The hair bulb surrounds the hair papilla, which is made of connective tissue and contains blood capillaries and nerve endings from the dermis.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1541120","f-f920adfee482"],["q5-f19bef0784f9","s5.2-7fd700ceab95","5.2","Hair","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nJust as the basal layer of the epidermis forms the layers of epidermis that get pushed to the surface as the dead skin on the surface sheds, the basal cells of the hair bulb divide and push cells outward in the ____ and shaft as the hair grows.","hair root",["sebaceous gland","glassy membrane","nail body"],"Just as the basal layer of the epidermis forms the layers of epidermis that get pushed to the surface as the dead skin on the surface sheds, the basal cells of the hair bulb divide and push cells outward in the hair root and shaft as the hair grows.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1319983","f-37255cdf6238"],["q5-e60af5ca9813","s5.2-4fc79783b47c","5.2","Hair","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe ____ forms the central core of the hair, which is surrounded by the cortex, a layer of compressed, keratinized cells that is covered by an outer layer of very hard, keratinized cells known as the cuticle.","medulla",["eponychium","telogen","keratin"],"The medulla forms the central core of the hair, which is surrounded by the cortex, a layer of compressed, keratinized cells that is covered by an outer layer of very hard, keratinized cells known as the cuticle.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1319983","f-fd8cd9516d22"],["q5-6ace1838b481","s5.2-f6b0a54c0899","5.2","Hair","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nHair growth begins with the production of keratinocytes by the basal cells of the ____.","hair bulb",["stratum basale","hair matrix","integumentary system"],"Hair growth begins with the production of keratinocytes by the basal cells of the hair bulb.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1319983","f-f936b683194d"],["q5-faa902b618f6","s5.2-eb244f8e3ff9","5.2","Hair","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nAs new cells are deposited at the hair bulb, the ____ is pushed through the follicle toward the surface.","hair shaft",["integumentary system","nail bed","nail cuticle"],"As new cells are deposited at the hair bulb, the hair shaft is pushed through the follicle toward the surface.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1319983","f-6b5099ce9805"],["q5-1b04dbefc787","s5.2-bc70b0511b26","5.2","Hair","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nKeratinization is completed as the cells are pushed to the skin surface to form the shaft of ____ that is externally visible.","hair",["eponychium","keratin","hypodermis"],"Keratinization is completed as the cells are pushed to the skin surface to form the shaft of hair that is externally visible.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1319983","f-bd6463383b1c"],["q5-3869e223f94b","s5.2-7e6bed95b9c6","5.2","Hair","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe external hair is completely dead and composed entirely of ____.","keratin",["telogen","epidermis","anagen"],"The external hair is completely dead and composed entirely of keratin.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1319983","f-0f00156106af"],["q5-348d178483b7","s5.2-76bbbc9db5e8","5.2","Hair","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe wall of the ____ is made of three concentric layers of cells.","hair follicle",["arrector pili","nail fold","hair matrix"],"The wall of the hair follicle is made of three concentric layers of cells.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1533651","f-180e432d769e"],["q5-198108fbe966","s5.2-dd544644a8cf","5.2","Hair","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe cells of the ____ surround the root of the growing hair and extend just up to the hair shaft.","internal root sheath",["eccrine sweat gland","external root sheath","apocrine sweat gland"],"The cells of the internal root sheath surround the root of the growing hair and extend just up to the hair shaft.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1533651","f-9a3bc729d472"],["q5-825aecefc41b","s5.2-08c5c1d4258d","5.2","Hair","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe ____, which is an extension of the epidermis, encloses the hair root.","external root sheath",["eccrine sweat gland","apocrine sweat gland","internal root sheath"],"The external root sheath, which is an extension of the epidermis, encloses the hair root.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1533651","f-28ade8b4e34a"],["q5-8cd3e0d836a7","s5.2-08c5c1d4258d","5.2","Hair","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe glassy membrane is the basement membrane that is found between the epithelium of the ____ and the connective tissue sheath.","external root sheath",["eccrine sweat gland","apocrine sweat gland","internal root sheath"],"The glassy membrane is the basement membrane that is found between the epithelium of the external root sheath and the connective tissue sheath.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1533651","f-98eba52b28c9"],["q5-c9a5f2c26f2a","s5.2-76bbbc9db5e8","5.2","Accessory Structures of the Skin","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe ____ is made of multiple layers of cells that form from basal cells in the hair matrix and the hair root.","hair follicle",["glassy membrane","hair papilla","hair shaft"],"The hair follicle is made of multiple layers of cells that form from basal cells in the hair matrix and the hair root.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1476432","f-9c7cda4c35f5"],["q5-87ffa5160bf7","s5.2-31eeb8e7f9c2","5.2","Accessory Structures of the Skin","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nCells of the ____ divide and differentiate to form the layers of the hair.","hair matrix",["hair papilla","hair root","nail body"],"Cells of the hair matrix divide and differentiate to form the layers of the hair.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1476432","f-6d240c1d7b4d"],["q5-0bb5077d68ac","s5.2-bc70b0511b26","5.2","Accessory Structures of the Skin","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\n____ serves a variety of functions, including protection, sensory input, thermoregulation, and communication.","Hair",["cortex","telogen","anagen"],"Hair serves a variety of functions, including protection, sensory input, thermoregulation, and communication.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1500108","f-1aab752198cc"],["q5-b4f6ef05c702","s5.2-bc70b0511b26","5.2","Accessory Structures of the Skin","application","Which term correctly completes this statement?\n____ on the head protects the skull from the sun.","hair",["catagen","sebum","telogen"],"For example, hair on the head protects the skull from the sun.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1500108","f-4640c83bd201"],["q5-ef206035e37b","s5.2-bc70b0511b26","5.2","Accessory Structures of the Skin","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe ____ in the nose and ears, and around the eyes (eyelashes) defends the body by trapping and excluding dust particles that may contain allergens and microbes.","hair",["hypodermis","melanin","catagen"],"The hair in the nose and ears, and around the eyes (eyelashes) defends the body by trapping and excluding dust particles that may contain allergens and microbes.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1500108","f-6e64bae736b5"],["q5-e03537ac4f29","s5.2-76bbbc9db5e8","5.2","Accessory Structures of the Skin","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nHair also has a sensory function due to sensory innervation by a hair root plexus surrounding the base of each ____.","hair follicle",["nail root","hair bulb","nail cuticle"],"Hair also has a sensory function due to sensory innervation by a hair root plexus surrounding the base of each hair follicle.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1500108","f-0b653d07fc7d"],["q5-b06e9483a406","s5.2-bc70b0511b26","5.2","Accessory Structures of the Skin","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\n____ is extremely sensitive to air movement or other disturbances in the environment, much more so than the skin surface.","Hair",["sebum","epidermis","hypodermis"],"Hair is extremely sensitive to air movement or other disturbances in the environment, much more so than the skin surface.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1500108","f-c705ba4601f6"],["q5-5fe8e29cb333","s5.2-eb244f8e3ff9","5.2","Hair Growth","application","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe first is the anagen phase, during which cells divide rapidly at the root of the hair, pushing the ____ up and out.","hair shaft",["integumentary system","hair matrix","glassy membrane"],"The first is the anagen phase, during which cells divide rapidly at the root of the hair, pushing the hair shaft up and out.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id961934","f-7b406f996791"],["q5-935fa40f8638","s5.2-76bbbc9db5e8","5.2","Hair Growth","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe catagen phase lasts only 2 to 3 weeks, and marks a transition from the ____’s active growth.","hair follicle",["hair shaft","nail body","nail root"],"The catagen phase lasts only 2 to 3 weeks, and marks a transition from the hair follicle’s active growth.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id961934","f-bcec6d4ae4f2"],["q5-a8d3343fe9bb","s5.2-76bbbc9db5e8","5.2","Hair Growth","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe basal cells in the hair matrix then produce a new ____, which pushes the old hair out as the growth cycle repeats itself.","hair follicle",["hair root","nail root","sebaceous gland"],"The basal cells in the hair matrix then produce a new hair follicle, which pushes the old hair out as the growth cycle repeats itself.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id961934","f-de0030161959"],["q5-045bdf949ca7","s5.2-1ac12aa01bca","5.2","Hair Growth","application","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nHair typically grows at the rate of 0.3 mm per day during the ____ phase.","anagen",["lunula","dermis","melanin"],"Hair typically grows at the rate of 0.3 mm per day during the anagen phase.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id961934","f-b12516808ea5"],["q5-446ad6f7ddbf","s5.2-853f525fcd76","5.2","Hair Color","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nDifferent hair color results from differences in the type of ____, which is genetically determined.","melanin",["cortex","dermis","hypodermis"],"Different hair color results from differences in the type of melanin, which is genetically determined.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1518349","f-f7d80584d0ca"],["q5-05b4eea6ce00","s5.2-5765ed8d7910","5.2","Nails","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe ____ is a specialized structure of the epidermis that is found at the tips of our fingers and toes.","nail bed",["hair matrix","nail body","integumentary system"],"The nail bed is a specialized structure of the epidermis that is found at the tips of our fingers and toes.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1200286","f-9d1d74e35b87"],["q5-5ce2e39522e3","s5.2-9c95b486d1e2","5.2","Nails","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe ____ forms a back-support for picking up small objects with the fingers.","nail body",["glassy membrane","arrector pili","nail root"],"In addition, the nail body forms a back-support for picking up small objects with the fingers.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1200286","f-8ed3e9851055"],["q5-006658e74d13","s5.2-9c95b486d1e2","5.2","Nails","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe ____ is composed of densely packed dead keratinocytes.","nail body",["sebaceous gland","nail fold","integumentary system"],"The nail body is composed of densely packed dead keratinocytes.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1200286","f-c6db5d07de2c"],["q5-9b9c075ad53c","s5.2-deb90a264323","5.2","Nails","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe nail body forms at the nail root, which has a matrix of proliferating cells from the ____ that enables the nail to grow continuously.","stratum basale",["nail bed","nail cuticle","integumentary system"],"The nail body forms at the nail root, which has a matrix of proliferating cells from the stratum basale that enables the nail to grow continuously.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1200286","f-cbc22408cdd5"],["q5-299ce1e652f1","s5.2-9c95b486d1e2","5.2","Nails","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe lateral nail fold overlaps the nail on the sides, helping to anchor the ____.","nail body",["glassy membrane","hair root","hair bulb"],"The lateral nail fold overlaps the nail on the sides, helping to anchor the nail body.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1200286","f-68da9f344b6d"],["q5-6f35544a3d27","s5.2-2b53e512dbc1","5.2","Nails","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe nail fold that meets the proximal end of the nail body forms the ____, also called the eponychium.","nail cuticle",["hair follicle","hair root","hair shaft"],"The nail fold that meets the proximal end of the nail body forms the nail cuticle, also called the eponychium.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1200286","f-16c676996611"],["q5-699c8f1a8b36","s5.2-90ab8ef22292","5.2","Nails","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe area beneath the free edge of the nail, furthest from the cuticle, is called the ____.","hyponychium",["sebum","cortex","melanin"],"The area beneath the free edge of the nail, furthest from the cuticle, is called the hyponychium.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1200286","f-407d5af8b918"],["q5-d774b167391c","s5.2-d964d993dc5a","5.2","Sweat Glands","application","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nWhen the body becomes warm, ____ produce sweat to cool the body.","sudoriferous glands",["arrector pili","integumentary system","nail fold"],"When the body becomes warm, sudoriferous glands produce sweat to cool the body.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1171634","f-a45bb0228453"],["q5-782d6c0d149e","s5.2-cecc8d5808c5","5.2","Sweat Glands","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nSweat glands develop from epidermal projections into the ____ and are classified as merocrine glands; that is, the secretions are excreted by exocytosis through a duct without affecting the cells of the gland.","dermis",["medulla","eponychium","anagen"],"Sweat glands develop from epidermal projections into the dermis and are classified as merocrine glands; that is, the secretions are excreted by exocytosis through a duct without affecting the cells of the gland.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1171634","f-9571d7861bb4"],["q5-7bc0cc3d8ec5","s5.2-7948b63a56f7","5.2","Sweat Glands","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nAn ____ is a type of gland that produces a hypotonic sweat for thermoregulation.","eccrine sweat gland",["external root sheath","internal root sheath","apocrine sweat gland"],"An eccrine sweat gland is a type of gland that produces a hypotonic sweat for thermoregulation.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1509858","f-2eb101de6c5e"],["q5-42b03fbee39d","s5.2-76bbbc9db5e8","5.2","Sweat Glands","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nApocrine sweat glands are larger than eccrine sweat glands and lie deeper in the dermis, sometimes even reaching the hypodermis, with the duct normally emptying into the ____.","hair follicle",["nail fold","nail bed","sebaceous gland"],"Apocrine sweat glands are larger than eccrine sweat glands and lie deeper in the dermis, sometimes even reaching the hypodermis, with the duct normally emptying into the hair follicle.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1449977","f-ec8b9caabb66"],["q5-3bf7f6fe088e","s5.2-5beda771f93c","5.2","Sebaceous Glands","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nA ____ is a type of oil gland that is found all over the body and helps to lubricate and waterproof the skin and hair.","sebaceous gland",["stratum corneum","nail fold","hair matrix"],"A sebaceous gland is a type of oil gland that is found all over the body and helps to lubricate and waterproof the skin and hair.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1107478","f-e73dc8d9b0e0"],["q5-324c36db337d","s5.2-bc70b0511b26","5.2","Sebaceous Glands","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nMost sebaceous glands are associated with ____ follicles.","hair",["cuticle","melanin","lunula"],"Most sebaceous glands are associated with hair follicles.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1107478","f-511cad33e5a0"],["q5-e63b209cbc59","s5.2-da28390c7c3d","5.2","Sebaceous Glands","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe fatty acids of ____ also have antibacterial properties, and prevent water loss from the skin in low-humidity environments.","sebum",["cortex","catagen","medulla"],"The fatty acids of sebum also have antibacterial properties, and prevent water loss from the skin in low-humidity environments.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1107478","f-5aca9ad52fce"],["q5-0ba03e058b81","s5.2-da28390c7c3d","5.2","Sebaceous Glands","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe secretion of ____ is stimulated by hormones, many of which do not become active until puberty.","sebum",["dermis","hair","anagen"],"The secretion of sebum is stimulated by hormones, many of which do not become active until puberty.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1107478","f-3079e20893c2"],["q5-8ae058fe6011","s5.3-09e51d9f22ee","5.3","Sensory Function","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\n(also, tactile corpuscle) receptor in the skin that responds to light touch","Meissner corpuscle",["stratum basale","Pacinian corpuscle","vitamin D"],"Meissner corpuscle: (also, tactile corpuscle) receptor in the skin that responds to light touch.","The answer begins with M and has 2 words.","fs-id1489872","f-23f6ddaab3b9"],["q5-2aa1de6fdd6d","s5.3-3cea92f7450f","5.3","Sensory Function","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\n(also, lamellated corpuscle) receptor in the skin that responds to vibration","Pacinian corpuscle",["hair root","Meissner corpuscle","arrector pili"],"Pacinian corpuscle: (also, lamellated corpuscle) receptor in the skin that responds to vibration.","The answer begins with P and has 2 words.","fs-id1489872","f-c3f4534e5742"],["q5-a59327bbc68c","s5.3-d0a871f8c15f","5.3","Vitamin D Synthesis","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\ndisease in children caused by vitamin D deficiency, which leads to the weakening of bones","rickets",["hair","epidermis","hypodermis"],"rickets: disease in children caused by vitamin D deficiency, which leads to the weakening of bones.","The answer begins with R and has 1 word.","fs-id1320162","f-72ee6048168d"],["q5-7676eae627b7","s5.3-542c255e9ec7","5.3","Tattoos and Piercings","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\ncollagen-rich skin formed after the process of wound healing that is different from normal skin","scar",["sebum","hypodermis","epidermis"],"scar: collagen-rich skin formed after the process of wound healing that is different from normal skin.","The answer begins with S and has 1 word.","fs-id1534723","f-2bf148b079f6"],["q5-5700f0d7f5bd","s5.3-ea0819c91eba","5.3","Functions of the Integumentary System","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe underlying ____ has important roles in storing fats, forming a “cushion” over underlying structures, and providing insulation from cold temperatures.","hypodermis",["hair","keratin","epidermis"],"The underlying hypodermis has important roles in storing fats, forming a “cushion” over underlying structures, and providing insulation from cold temperatures.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1554404","f-a4badb657223"],["q5-17c92fba0ba1","s5.3-76bbbc9db5e8","5.3","Sensory Function","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe hair root plexus surrounding the base of the ____ senses a disturbance, and then transmits the information to the central nervous system (brain and spinal cord), which can then respond by activating the skeletal muscles of your eyes to see the ant and the skeletal muscles of the body to act against the ant.","hair follicle",["vitamin D","Pacinian corpuscle","arrector pili"],"The hair root plexus surrounding the base of the hair follicle senses a disturbance, and then transmits the information to the central nervous system (brain and spinal cord), which can then respond by activating the skeletal muscles of your eyes to see the ant and the skeletal muscles of the body to act against the ant.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1403931","f-fe1375f669e2"],["q5-b65db34e2187","s5.3-ea0819c91eba","5.3","Sensory Function","application","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe skin acts as a sense organ because the epidermis, dermis, and the ____ contain specialized sensory nerve structures that detect touch, surface temperature, and pain.","hypodermis",["rickets","hair","sebum"],"The skin acts as a sense organ because the epidermis, dermis, and the hypodermis contain specialized sensory nerve structures that detect touch, surface temperature, and pain.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1489872","f-39a793b0abbd"],["q5-f88757fecfa6","s5.3-cecc8d5808c5","5.3","Integumentary System","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe ____, which is responsible for the elasticity and resilience of the skin, exhibits a reduced ability to regenerate, which leads to slower wound healing.","dermis",["keratin","scar","rickets"],"The dermis, which is responsible for the elasticity and resilience of the skin, exhibits a reduced ability to regenerate, which leads to slower wound healing.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1570487","f-1e9af801d402"],["q5-3c17632070d8","s5.3-da28390c7c3d","5.3","Integumentary System","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe accessory structures also have lowered activity, generating thinner hair and nails, and reduced amounts of ____ and sweat.","sebum",["dermis","hypodermis","scar"],"The accessory structures also have lowered activity, generating thinner hair and nails, and reduced amounts of sebum and sweat.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1527677","f-e44a7015b549"],["q5-756d08ecd94f","s5.3-8c56c31fbb78","5.3","Vitamin D Synthesis","application","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe epidermal layer of human skin synthesizes ____ when exposed to UV radiation.","vitamin D",["dermal papilla","hair follicle","Meissner corpuscle"],"The epidermal layer of human skin synthesizes vitamin D when exposed to UV radiation.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1320162","f-2bccc8796f03"],["q5-248b99697abc","s5.3-8c56c31fbb78","5.3","Vitamin D Synthesis","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nIn the presence of sunlight, a form of ____ 3 called cholecalciferol is synthesized from a derivative of the steroid cholesterol in the skin.","vitamin D",["integumentary system","arrector pili","dermal papilla"],"In the presence of sunlight, a form of vitamin D 3 called cholecalciferol is synthesized from a derivative of the steroid cholesterol in the skin.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1320162","f-1e7f4821c045"],["q5-b0086690d739","s5.3-8c56c31fbb78","5.3","Vitamin D Synthesis","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\n____ is essential for normal absorption of calcium and phosphorous, which are required for healthy bones.","Vitamin D",["stratum basale","stratum corneum","arrector pili"],"Vitamin D is essential for normal absorption of calcium and phosphorous, which are required for healthy bones.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1320162","f-c0282ba3aaff"],["q5-6b4e0d3a2614","s5.3-8c56c31fbb78","5.3","Vitamin D Synthesis","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe absence of sun exposure can lead to a lack of ____ in the body, leading to a condition called rickets, a painful condition in children where the bones are misshapen due to a lack of calcium, causing bowleggedness.","vitamin D",["stratum basale","Pacinian corpuscle","hair follicle"],"The absence of sun exposure can lead to a lack of vitamin D in the body, leading to a condition called rickets, a painful condition in children where the bones are misshapen due to a lack of calcium, causing bowleggedness.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1320162","f-0740f7719dd8"],["q5-fbea531fabc8","s5.3-8c56c31fbb78","5.3","Vitamin D Synthesis","application","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nElderly individuals who suffer from ____ deficiency can develop a condition called osteomalacia, a softening of the bones.","vitamin D",["Pacinian corpuscle","hair follicle","arrector pili"],"Elderly individuals who suffer from vitamin D deficiency can develop a condition called osteomalacia, a softening of the bones.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1320162","f-9234eb371221"],["q5-5ac5094ced3c","s5.3-8c56c31fbb78","5.3","Vitamin D Synthesis","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nIn present day society, ____ is added as a supplement to many foods, including milk and orange juice, compensating for the need for sun exposure.","vitamin D",["Meissner corpuscle","dermal papilla","Pacinian corpuscle"],"In present day society, vitamin D is added as a supplement to many foods, including milk and orange juice, compensating for the need for sun exposure.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1320162","f-426aa94c41b9"],["q5-22873499991a","s5.4-cc0dd2d73e27","5.4","Skin Disorders","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nskin condition due to infected sebaceous glands","acne",["metastasis","keloid","melanin"],"acne: skin condition due to infected sebaceous glands.","The answer begins with A and has 1 word.","fs-id1943902","f-2f77275d9800"],["q5-380570f71098","s5.4-826fad939211","5.4","Basal Cell Carcinoma","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\ncancer that originates from basal cells in the epidermis of the skin","basal cell carcinoma",["squamous cell carcinoma","sebum","integumentary system"],"basal cell carcinoma: cancer that originates from basal cells in the epidermis of the skin.","The answer begins with B and has 3 words.","fs-id1124918","f-adf03aeb6ed3"],["q5-def61bb53083","s5.4-e2eaaedbf42f","5.4","Bedsores and Stretch Marks","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nsore on the skin that develops when regions of the body start necrotizing due to constant pressure and lack of blood supply; also called decubitus ulcers","bedsore",["scar","sebum","keratin"],"bedsore: sore on the skin that develops when regions of the body start necrotizing due to constant pressure and lack of blood supply; also called decubitus ulcers.","The answer begins with B and has 1 word.","fs-id1942665","f-9b0364bf06ce"],["q5-185ace6dbdc2","s5.4-3b0dca5ef4ee","5.4","Calluses","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nthickened area of skin that arises due to constant abrasion","callus",["keloid","corn","acne"],"callus: thickened area of skin that arises due to constant abrasion.","The answer begins with C and has 1 word.","fs-id1942692","f-1565eab5d7b5"],["q5-cdadafaf813f","s5.4-7cacb75c4cc3","5.4","Calluses","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\ntype of callus that is named for its shape and the elliptical motion of the abrasive force","corn",["dermis","metastasis","sebum"],"corn: type of callus that is named for its shape and the elliptical motion of the abrasive force.","The answer begins with C and has 1 word.","fs-id1942692","f-3ae540c8dc6c"],["q5-12a938551331","s5.4-435846e52b2d","5.4","Skin Disorders","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nskin condition due to an allergic reaction, which resembles a rash","eczema",["dermis","keloid","corn"],"eczema: skin condition due to an allergic reaction, which resembles a rash.","The answer begins with E and has 1 word.","fs-id1943902","f-2fcf609df872"],["q5-8978ce75c2ec","s5.4-a97fd7fa96aa","5.4","Burns","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nsuperficial burn that injures only the epidermis","first-degree burn",["integumentary system","stratum spinosum","second-degree burn"],"first-degree burn: superficial burn that injures only the epidermis.","The answer begins with F and has 2 words.","fs-id1942557","f-6dd039c1cfcd"],["q5-354a4b03c372","s5.4-2c7f0d2017ca","5.4","Burns","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nburn in which full thickness of the skin and underlying muscle and bone is damaged","fourth-degree burn",["stratum spinosum","stratum basale","stretch mark"],"fourth-degree burn: burn in which full thickness of the skin and underlying muscle and bone is damaged.","The answer begins with F and has 2 words.","fs-id1942557","f-3b494338d398"],["q5-ca10cc6d49ee","s5.4-4abe27fe6dad","5.4","Scars and Keloids","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\ntype of scar that has layers raised above the skin surface","keloid",["hair","corn","melanin"],"keloid: type of scar that has layers raised above the skin surface.","The answer begins with K and has 1 word.","fs-id1942644","f-edc90261a39f"],["q5-6b6eacf66a0b","s5.4-9ab47e738d58","5.4","Melanoma","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\ntype of skin cancer that originates from the melanocytes of the skin","melanoma",["corn","keratin","scar"],"melanoma: type of skin cancer that originates from the melanocytes of the skin.","The answer begins with M and has 1 word.","fs-id1521254","f-1a0c3859f167"],["q5-490051b4f097","s5.4-09f08971b0be","5.4","Diseases","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nspread of cancer cells from a source to other parts of the body","metastasis",["scar","hair","keloid"],"metastasis: spread of cancer cells from a source to other parts of the body.","The answer begins with M and has 1 word.","fs-id691867","f-701fa50d35cb"],["q5-87a08054062d","s5.4-42337cb19e86","5.4","Burns","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\npartial-thickness burn that injures the epidermis and a portion of the dermis","second-degree burn",["stratum spinosum","stratum basale","fourth-degree burn"],"second-degree burn: partial-thickness burn that injures the epidermis and a portion of the dermis.","The answer begins with S and has 2 words.","fs-id1942557","f-378494b97898"],["q5-9148dc8c809d","s5.4-9b68193ac15b","5.4","Squamous Cell Carcinoma","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\ntype of skin cancer that originates from the stratum spinosum of the epidermis","squamous cell carcinoma",["basal cell carcinoma","hair","stretch mark"],"squamous cell carcinoma: type of skin cancer that originates from the stratum spinosum of the epidermis.","The answer begins with S and has 3 words.","fs-id1943755","f-4f6dd374a5d2"],["q5-d78101e1658d","s5.4-3239fd444f9f","5.4","Bedsores and Stretch Marks","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nmark formed on the skin due to a sudden growth spurt and expansion of the dermis beyond its elastic limits","stretch mark",["stratum spinosum","basal cell","first-degree burn"],"stretch mark: mark formed on the skin due to a sudden growth spurt and expansion of the dermis beyond its elastic limits.","The answer begins with S and has 2 words.","fs-id1942676","f-7248ea77dfca"],["q5-9370cac78a0f","s5.4-599b3fc05e01","5.4","Burns","foundations","Which term matches this definition?\nburn that penetrates and destroys the full thickness of the skin (epidermis and dermis)","third-degree burn",["basal cell","stratum basale","first-degree burn"],"third-degree burn: burn that penetrates and destroys the full thickness of the skin (epidermis and dermis).","The answer begins with T and has 2 words.","fs-id1942557","f-09658bdf283d"],["q5-6b1d0d4400bb","s5.4-c8879414c447","5.4","Diseases, Disorders, and Injuries of the Integumentary System","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe ____ is susceptible to a variety of diseases, disorders, and injuries.","integumentary system",["first-degree burn","fourth-degree burn","second-degree burn"],"The integumentary system is susceptible to a variety of diseases, disorders, and injuries.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1734070","f-aed9be873183"],["q5-7036c7118204","s5.4-826fad939211","5.4","Basal Cell Carcinoma","application","Which term correctly completes this statement?\n____ is a form of cancer that affects the mitotically active stem cells in the stratum basale of the epidermis.","Basal cell carcinoma",["squamous cell carcinoma","integumentary system","bedsore"],"Basal cell carcinoma is a form of cancer that affects the mitotically active stem cells in the stratum basale of the epidermis.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1124918","f-63f44c85ee81"],["q5-c01a7deb3c0f","s5.4-7162eeffe485","5.4","Basal Cell Carcinoma","application","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nLike most cancers, ____ carcinomas respond best to treatment when caught early.","basal cell",["first-degree burn","stratum spinosum","integumentary system"],"Like most cancers, basal cell carcinomas respond best to treatment when caught early.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1124918","f-10a51d809e82"],["q5-bc162fc698b2","s5.4-9b68193ac15b","5.4","Squamous Cell Carcinoma","application","Which term correctly completes this statement?\n____ is a cancer that affects the keratinocytes of the stratum spinosum and presents as lesions commonly found on the scalp, ears, and hands.","squamous cell carcinoma",["basal cell carcinoma","integumentary system","eczema"],"Squamous cell carcinoma is a cancer that affects the keratinocytes of the stratum spinosum and presents as lesions commonly found on the scalp, ears, and hands.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1943755","f-96fafde0385a"],["q5-d59fcac0810a","s5.4-9b68193ac15b","5.4","Squamous Cell Carcinoma","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nSurgery and radiation are used to cure ____.","squamous cell carcinoma",["basal cell carcinoma","bedsore","first-degree burn"],"Surgery and radiation are used to cure squamous cell carcinoma.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1943755","f-285d30e88f47"],["q5-ca9479a34ea2","s5.4-bafd3e0b93aa","5.4","Melanoma","application","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nA melanoma is a cancer characterized by the uncontrolled growth of melanocytes, the pigment-producing cells in the ____.","epidermis",["hair","callus","keloid"],"A melanoma is a cancer characterized by the uncontrolled growth of melanocytes, the pigment-producing cells in the epidermis.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1521254","f-0e970fb7e4a2"],["q5-0219d5d60d8e","s5.4-435846e52b2d","5.4","Skin Disorders","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nTwo common skin disorders are ____ and acne.","eczema",["sebum","melanin","keratin"],"Two common skin disorders are eczema and acne.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1943902","f-1b868b7d64e6"],["q5-29003f069db3","s5.4-435846e52b2d","5.4","Skin Disorders","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\n____ is an inflammatory condition and occurs in individuals of all ages.","Eczema",["callus","bedsore","hair"],"Eczema is an inflammatory condition and occurs in individuals of all ages.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1943902","f-62bf5883b057"],["q5-47825bc3412e","s5.4-cc0dd2d73e27","5.4","Skin Disorders","application","Which term correctly completes this statement?\n____ involves the clogging of pores, which can lead to infection and inflammation, and is often seen in adolescents.","Acne",["sebum","dermis","callus"],"Acne involves the clogging of pores, which can lead to infection and inflammation, and is often seen in adolescents.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1943902","f-6dad55cd65c7"],["q5-30391386482a","s5.4-435846e52b2d","5.4","Eczema","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\n____ is an allergic reaction that manifests as dry, itchy patches of skin that resemble rashes.","Eczema",["epidermis","sebum","corn"],"Eczema is an allergic reaction that manifests as dry, itchy patches of skin that resemble rashes.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1943913","f-807c1dc0784e"],["q5-125a0773abf0","s5.4-cc0dd2d73e27","5.4","Acne","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\n____ is a skin disturbance that typically occurs on areas of the skin that are rich in sebaceous glands (face and back).","Acne",["keratin","hair","epidermis"],"Acne is a skin disturbance that typically occurs on areas of the skin that are rich in sebaceous glands (face and back).","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1618855","f-687b51c62a48"],["q5-a5130f22bbbc","s5.4-7e6bed95b9c6","5.4","Acne","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nAn overproduction and accumulation of sebum along with ____ can block hair follicles.","keratin",["melanin","corn","epidermis"],"An overproduction and accumulation of sebum along with keratin can block hair follicles.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1618855","f-cb409e4ee543"],["q5-97342415f561","s5.4-da28390c7c3d","5.4","Acne","application","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nThe ____, when oxidized by exposure to air, turns black.","sebum",["dermis","bedsore","metastasis"],"The sebum, when oxidized by exposure to air, turns black.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1618855","f-a879909777d2"],["q5-e212bd70ba4d","s5.4-deb90a264323","5.4","Injuries","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nBefore the basal stem cells of the ____ can recreate the epidermis, fibroblasts mobilize and divide rapidly to repair the damaged tissue by collagen deposition, forming granulation tissue.","stratum basale",["integumentary system","stratum spinosum","second-degree burn"],"Before the basal stem cells of the stratum basale can recreate the epidermis, fibroblasts mobilize and divide rapidly to repair the damaged tissue by collagen deposition, forming granulation tissue.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1541614","f-eda0a93c7587"],["q5-537360563c14","s5.4-f9a90f6f41a7","5.4","Burns","application","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nBurn patients are treated with intravenous fluids to offset ____, as well as intravenous nutrients that enable the body to repair tissues and replace lost proteins.","dehydration",["melanin","metastasis","dermis"],"Burn patients are treated with intravenous fluids to offset dehydration, as well as intravenous nutrients that enable the body to repair tissues and replace lost proteins.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1942548","f-8b14ca6fd86f"],["q5-b61914027713","s5.4-a97fd7fa96aa","5.4","Burns","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nA ____ is a superficial burn that affects only the epidermis.","first-degree burn",["stretch mark","fourth-degree burn","basal cell"],"A first-degree burn is a superficial burn that affects only the epidermis.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1942557","f-1c8813fba85a"],["q5-52245fbbaf01","s5.4-a97fd7fa96aa","5.4","Burns","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nMild sunburn fits into the category of a ____.","first-degree burn",["stratum spinosum","basal cell","stretch mark"],"Mild sunburn fits into the category of a first-degree burn.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1942557","f-22cd07397bc1"],["q5-0a9c530d1240","s5.4-42337cb19e86","5.4","Burns","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nA ____ goes deeper and affects both the epidermis and a portion of the dermis.","second-degree burn",["third-degree burn","stratum spinosum","fourth-degree burn"],"A second-degree burn goes deeper and affects both the epidermis and a portion of the dermis.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1942557","f-f4fc9dabeb0f"],["q5-dc3affefba6f","s5.4-2c7f0d2017ca","5.4","Burns","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nA ____ is even more severe, affecting the underlying muscle and bone.","fourth-degree burn",["basal cell","integumentary system","stratum basale"],"A fourth-degree burn is even more severe, affecting the underlying muscle and bone.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1942557","f-39115335a32b"],["q5-fc77bf0db5ee","s5.4-bafd3e0b93aa","5.4","Scars and Keloids","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nMost cuts or wounds, with the exception of ones that only scratch the surface (the ____), lead to scar formation.","epidermis",["keloid","melanoma","melanin"],"Most cuts or wounds, with the exception of ones that only scratch the surface (the epidermis), lead to scar formation.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1942631","f-b108d7317368"],["q5-9a9f8c0b9123","s5.4-542c255e9ec7","5.4","Scars and Keloids","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nA ____ is collagen-rich skin formed after the process of wound healing that differs from normal skin.","scar",["callus","keloid","acne"],"A scar is collagen-rich skin formed after the process of wound healing that differs from normal skin.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1942631","f-1c814accab08"],["q5-fa08f8c5ca95","s5.4-542c255e9ec7","5.4","Scars and Keloids","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nFibroblasts generate ____ tissue in the form of collagen, and the bulk of repair is due to the basket-weave pattern generated by collagen fibers and does not result in regeneration of the typical cellular structure of skin.","scar",["melanin","hair","keratin"],"Fibroblasts generate scar tissue in the form of collagen, and the bulk of repair is due to the basket-weave pattern generated by collagen fibers and does not result in regeneration of the typical cellular structure of skin.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1942631","f-b9dba4434c35"],["q5-86d302096247","s5.4-cc0dd2d73e27","5.4","Scars and Keloids","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nScars that result from ____ and chickenpox have a sunken appearance and are called atrophic scars.","acne",["metastasis","eczema","epidermis"],"In contrast, scars that result from acne and chickenpox have a sunken appearance and are called atrophic scars.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1942644","f-20bc765fb96d"],["q5-56a241c883ce","s5.4-542c255e9ec7","5.4","Scars and Keloids","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nApplication of mineral oil and lotions may reduce the formation of ____ tissue.","scar",["keratin","dermis","metastasis"],"Application of mineral oil and lotions may reduce the formation of scar tissue.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1942651","f-3735cfd7740e"],["q5-8ea90ebc50eb","s5.4-3b0dca5ef4ee","5.4","Calluses","application","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nWhen you wear shoes that do not fit well and are a constant source of abrasion on your toes, you tend to form a ____ at the point of contact.","callus",["corn","bedsore","hair"],"When you wear shoes that do not fit well and are a constant source of abrasion on your toes, you tend to form a callus at the point of contact.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1942692","f-dd8506520058"],["q5-bc5295a18065","s5.4-3b0dca5ef4ee","5.4","Calluses","connections","Which term correctly completes this statement?\nA corn is a specialized form of ____.","callus",["melanin","melanoma","sebum"],"A corn is a specialized form of callus.","Identify the structure, process, or substance that fits the role described in the statement.","fs-id1942692","f-10226cdaf076"],["q5-39aa1635d098","s5.3-b707035de90a","5.3","Protection","connections","Which skin components help limit water loss at the surface?","Keratin and glycolipids in the stratum corneum",["Ventricular valves and chordae","Bile and pancreatic enzymes","Alveolar surfactant and pleura"],"The keratinized outer epidermal barrier and its lipids reduce water loss.","Identify the structure or mechanism named in the question, then compare the alternatives.","fs-id1709565","f-bc3f6eeb4962"],["q5-5503fb39a4b7","s5.4-bc55b2b10099","5.4","Dermatologist","connections","Which specialist diagnoses and treats disorders of the skin?","Dermatologist",["Cardiologist","Nephrologist","Neurologist"],"Dermatology focuses on skin disorders and related conditions.","Identify the structure or mechanism named in the question, then compare the alternatives.","fs-id1943991","f-47d1979a87d2"],["q5-25383a7183a9","s5.4-c062a3748ca0","5.4","Dermatologist","application","A professional evaluates a concerning mole and persistent skin rash. Which specialty is most directly described?","Dermatology",["Cardiology","Vascular surgery","Forensic anthropology"],"These examples concern the skin and illustrate the work of a dermatologist.","Identify the structure or mechanism named in the question, then compare the alternatives.","fs-id1943991","f-0c08996db352"],["q5-edit-221fc25de3c5","s5.3-edit-ba70b57e065d","5.3","Thermoregulation","connections","Which skin responses promote heat loss when body temperature rises?","Increased sweating and dilation of skin blood vessels",["Reduced sweating and constriction of skin blood vessels","Increased melanin synthesis and nail growth","Decreased skin blood flow and increased hair growth"],"Sweat evaporation and increased blood flow near the skin surface help release body heat.","Use the role or mechanism described in the question.","fs-id1239604","f-12fc1156084d"]]);
